[4303.040882, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[13S\u001b[13A\u001b[4mTCPDUMP\u001b(B\u001b[m(8)                                                                        System Manager's Manual                                                                       \u001b[4mTCPDUMP\u001b(B\u001b[m(8)\u001b[20;1H\u001b[1mNAME\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m       tcpdump - dump traffic on a network\u001b[23;1H\u001b[1mSYNOPSIS\r\n\u001b(B\u001b[m       \u001b[1mtcpdump \u001b(B\u001b[m[ \u001b[1m-AbdDefhHIJKlLnNOpqStuUvxX# \u001b(B\u001b[m] [ \u001b[1m-B \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mbuffer_size\u001b(B\u001b[m ]\r\n               [ \u001b[1m-c \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mcount\u001b(B\u001b[m ] [ \u001b[1m--count \u001b(B\u001b[m] [ \u001b[1m-C \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mfile_size\u001b(B\u001b[m ]\r\n               [ \u001b[1m-E \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mspi@ipaddr\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4malgo:secret,...\u001b(B\u001b[m  ]\u001b[K\r\n               [ \u001b[1m-F \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mfile\u001b(B\u001b[m ] [ \u001b[1m-G \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mrotate_seconds\u001b(B\u001b[m ] [ \u001b[1m-i \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4minterface\u001b(B\u001b[m ]\u001b[K\r\n               [ \u001b[1m--immediate-mode \u001b(B\u001b[m] [ \u001b[1m-j \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mtstamp_type\u001b(B\u001b[m ] [ \u001b[1m-m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mmodule\u001b(B\u001b[m ]\u001b[K\r\n               [ \u001b[1m-M \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4msecret\u001b(B\u001b[m ] [ \u001b[1m--number \u001b(B\u001b[m] [ \u001b[1m--print \u001b(B\u001b[m] [ \u001b[1m-Q \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4min|out|inout\u001b(B\u001b[m ]\u001b[K\r\n               [ \u001b[1m-r \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mfile\u001b(B\u001b[m ] [ \u001b[1m-s \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4msnaplen\u001b(B\u001b[m ] [ \u001b[1m-T \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mtype\u001b(B\u001b[m ] [ \u001b[1m--version \u001b(B\u001b[m]\u001b[K\r\n               [ \u001b[1m-V \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mfile\u001b(B\u001b[m ] [ \u001b[1m-w \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mfile\u001b(B\u001b[m ] [ \u001b[1m-W \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mfilecount\u001b(B\u001b[m ] [ \u001b[1m-y \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mdatalinktype\u001b(B\u001b[m ]\u001b[K\r\n               [ \u001b[1m-z \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mpostrotate-command\u001b(B\u001b[m ] [ \u001b[1m-Z \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4muser\u001b(B\u001b[m ]\u001b[K\r\n               [ \u001b[1m--time-stamp-precision=\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4mtstamp_precision\u001b(B\u001b[m ]\u001b[K\r\n               [ \u001b[1m--micro \u001b(B\u001b[m] [ \u001b[1m--nano \u001b(B\u001b[m]\u001b[K\r\n               [ \u001b[4mexpression\u001b(B\u001b[m ]\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[1mDESCRIPTION\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n       \u001b[4mTcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m  prints out a description of the contents of packets on a network interface that match the Boolean \u001b[4mexpression\u001b(B\u001b[m; the description is preceded by a time stamp, printed, by de\u001b[K‐\r\u001b[5S\u001b[4A       fault, as hours, minutes, seconds, and fractions of a second since midnight.  It can also be run with the \u001b[1m-w \u001b(B\u001b[mflag, which causes it to save the packet data  to  a  file  for  later\u001b[K\r\n       analysis,  and/or  with  the  \u001b[1m-r \u001b(B\u001b[mflag, which causes it to read from a saved packet file rather than to read packets from a network interface.  It can also be run with the \u001b[1m-V \u001b(B\u001b[mflag,\u001b[K\r\n       which causes it to read a list of saved packet files. In all cases, only packets that match \u001b[4mexpression\u001b(B\u001b[m will be processed by \u001b[4mtcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n       \u001b[4mTcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m will, if not run with the \u001b[1m-c \u001b(B\u001b[mflag, continue capturing packets until it is interrupted by a SIGINT signal (generated, for example, by typing your interrupt character, typi\u001b[K‐\r\u001b[8S\u001b[7A       cally control-C) or a SIGTERM signal (typically generated with the \u001b[1mkill\u001b(B\u001b[m(1) command); if run with the \u001b[1m-c \u001b(B\u001b[mflag, it will capture packets until  it  is  interrupted  by  a  SIGINT  or\u001b[K\r\n       SIGTERM signal or the specified number of packets have been processed.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n       When \u001b[4mtcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m finishes capturing packets, it will report counts of:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n              packets ``captured'' (this is the number of packets that \u001b[4mtcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m has received and processed);\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n              packets ``received by filter'' (the meaning of this depends on the OS on which you're running \u001b[4mtcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m, and possibly on the way the OS was configured - if a filter was spec\u001b[K‐\r\n              ified  on the command line, on some OSes it counts packets regardless of whether they were matched by the filter expression and, even if they were matched by the filter ex\u001b[K‐\r\u001b[3S\u001b[2A              pression, regardless of whether \u001b[4mtcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m has read and processed them yet, on other OSes it counts only packets that were matched  by  the  filter  expression  regardless  of\u001b[K\r\n              whether \u001b[4mtcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m has read and processed them yet, and on other OSes it counts only packets that were matched by the filter expression and were processed by \u001b[4mtcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m);\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 1 (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[?2026l"]
