[4310.619941, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[20;1H\u001b[32m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[2 q\u001b[?25l\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1;8H\u001b[1K\u001b[C0x0020:  8011 1000 8425 0000 0101 080a 1a1c d37f  .....%..........\u001b[K\u001b[2;8H\u001b[1K\u001b[C0x0030:  e0cd cca5                                ....\u001b[K\r\n12:12:17.005859 IP (tos 0x0, ttl 64, id 34140, offset 0, flags [DF], proto TCP (6), length 52)\u001b[K\r\n    candy_shop.com.40292 > 114.29.233.106.static.gitipl.com.5001: Flags [.], cksum 0xe0d6 (incorrect -> 0x922a), seq 85, ack 735, win 504, options [nop,nop,TS val 3771583656 ecr 438096767], length 0\u001b[K\u001b[6;8H\u001b[1K\u001b[C0x0000:  4500 0034 855c 4000 4006 d4b7 ac14 d913  E..4.\\@.@.......\u001b[K\u001b[7;8H\u001b[1K\u001b[C0x0010:  721d e96a 9d64 1389 aa40 70b1 f48f a668  r..j.d...@p....h\u001b[K\u001b[8;8H\u001b[1K\u001b[C0x0020:  8010 01f8 e0d6 0000 0101 080a e0cd cca8  ................\u001b[K\u001b[9;8H\u001b[1K\u001b[C0x0030:  1a1c d37f                                ....\u001b[K\r\n^C\u001b[K\r\n10 packets captured\u001b[K\r\n10 packets received by filter\u001b[K\r\n0 packets dropped by kernel\u001b[K\u001b[33m\u001b[1m\r\nhrutvik_\u001b(B\u001b[m in \u001b[32m\u001b[1m\u001b[2m🌐 ArbinIndia-Hrutvik\u001b(B\u001b[m in \u001b[36m\u001b[1m~/pers/protocols\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[32m\u001b[1m❯\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[32m\u001b[4msudo\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[32mtcpdump\u001b[39m -i eth0 -vv -s0 -w /tmp/test-capture-entire-http.pcap tcp port 5001\u001b[39X\u001b[39Ctook \u001b[33m\u001b[1m5m38s\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[K\r\ntcpdump: listening on eth0, link-type EN10MB (Ethernet), snapshot length 262144 bytes\u001b[K\r\n^C9 packets captured\u001b[K\r\n9 packets received by filter\u001b[K\r\n0 packets dropped by kernel\u001b[K\u001b[33m\u001b[1m\r\nhrutvik_\u001b(B\u001b[m in \u001b[32m\u001b[1m\u001b[2m🌐 ArbinIndia-Hrutvik\u001b(B\u001b[m in \u001b[36m\u001b[1m~/pers/protocols\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[32m\u001b[1m❯\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[121X\u001b[121Ctook \u001b[33m\u001b[1m18s\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[K\u001b[2 q\u001b[?25l\u001b[21;1H       \u001b[4mTcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m  prints out a description of the contents of packets on a network interface that match the Boolean \u001b[4mexpression\u001b(B\u001b[m; the description is preceded by a time stamp, printed, by de‐\u001b[K\r\n       fault, as hours, minutes, seconds, and fractions of a second since midnight.  It can also be run with the \u001b[1m-w \u001b(B\u001b[mflag, which causes it to save the packet data  to  a  file  for  later\u001b[K\r\n       analysis,  and/or  with  the  \u001b[1m-r \u001b(B\u001b[mflag, which causes it to read from a saved packet file rather than to read packets from a network interface.  It can also be run with the \u001b[1m-V \u001b(B\u001b[mflag,\u001b[K\r\n       which causes it to read a list of saved packet files. In all cases, only packets that match \u001b[4mexpression\u001b(B\u001b[m will be processed by \u001b[4mtcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n       \u001b[4mTcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m will, if not run with the \u001b[1m-c \u001b(B\u001b[mflag, continue capturing packets until it is interrupted by a SIGINT signal (generated, for example, by typing your interrupt character, typi‐\u001b[K\r\n       cally control-C) or a SIGTERM signal (typically generated with the \u001b[1mkill\u001b(B\u001b[m(1) command); if run with the \u001b[1m-c \u001b(B\u001b[mflag, it will capture packets until  it  is  interrupted  by  a  SIGINT  or\u001b[K\r\n       SIGTERM signal or the specified number of packets have been processed.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n       When \u001b[4mtcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m finishes capturing packets, it will report counts of:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n              packets ``captured'' (this is the number of packets that \u001b[4mtcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m has received and processed);\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n              packets ``received by filter'' (the meaning of this depends on the OS on which you're running \u001b[4mtcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m, and possibly on the way the OS was configured - if a filter was spec‐\u001b[K\r\n              ified  on the command line, on some OSes it counts packets regardless of whether they were matched by the filter expression and, even if they were matched by the filter ex‐\u001b[K\r\n              pression, regardless of whether \u001b[4mtcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m h"]
