[4380.634815, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[2 q\u001b[?25l       >  separating  the source and destination.  For other protocols, the addresses will be printed, with a > separating the source and destination.  Higher level protocol information,\u001b[K\r\n       if any, will be printed after that.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n       For fragmented IP datagrams, the first fragment contains the higher level protocol header; fragments after the first contain no higher level protocol header.  Fragmentation infor‐\u001b[K\r\n       mation will be printed only with the \u001b[1m-v \u001b(B\u001b[mflag, in the IP header information, as described above.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n       \u001b[1mTCP Packets\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n       \u001b[4m(N.B.:The\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mfollowing\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mdescription\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4massumes\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mfamiliarity\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mwith\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mthe\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mTCP\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mprotocol\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mdescribed\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4min\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mRFC-793.\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[4mIf\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4myou\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mare\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mnot\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mfamiliar\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mwith\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mthe\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mprotocol,\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mthis\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mdescription\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mwill\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mnot\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[4mbe\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[4mof\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[4mmuch\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n       \u001b[4muse\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4mto\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[4myou.)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n       The general format of a TCP protocol line is:\u001b[K\r\n              \u001b[4msrc\u001b(B\u001b[m > \u001b[4mdst\u001b(B\u001b[m: Flags [\u001b[4mtcpflags\u001b(B\u001b[m], seq \u001b[4mdata-seqno\u001b(B\u001b[m, ack \u001b[4mackno\u001b(B\u001b[m, win \u001b[4mwindow\u001b(B\u001b[m, urg \u001b[4murgent\u001b(B\u001b[m, options [\u001b[4mopts\u001b(B\u001b[m], length \u001b[4mlen\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n       \u001b[4mSrc\u001b(B\u001b[m and \u001b[4mdst\u001b(B\u001b[m are the source and destination IP addresses and ports.  \u001b[4mTcpflags\u001b(B\u001b[m are some combination of S (SYN), F (FIN), P (PUSH), R (RST), U (URG), W (ECN CWR), E (ECN-Echo) or `.'\u001b[K\r\n       (ACK),  or `none' if no flags are set.  \u001b[4mData-seqno\u001b(B\u001b[m describes the portion of sequence space covered by the data in this packet (see example below).  \u001b[4mAckno\u001b(B\u001b[m is sequence number of the\u001b[K\r\n       next data expected the other direction on this connection.  \u001b[4mWindow\u001b(B\u001b[m is the number of bytes of receive buffer space available the other direction on this connection.  \u001b[4mUrg\u001b(B\u001b[m  indicates\u001b[K\r\n       there is `urgent' data in the packet.  \u001b[4mOpts\u001b(B\u001b[m are TCP options (e.g., mss 1024).  \u001b[4mLen\u001b(B\u001b[m is the length of payload data.\u001b[K\u001b[7m\r\n Manual page tcpdump(8) line 488/904 59% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[20;1H──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[32m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
