[4425.41595, "o", "\r       The  first line says that TCP port 1023 on rtsg sent a packet to port \u001b[4mlogin\u001b(B\u001b[m on csam.  The \u001b[1mS \u001b(B\u001b[mindicates that the \u001b[4mSYN\u001b(B\u001b[m flag was set.  The packet sequence number was 768512 and it con\u001b[?2026h\u001b[K‐\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 502/904 61% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
[4425.433195, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[A       tained no data.  (The notation is `first:last' which means `sequence numbers \u001b[4mfirst\u001b(B\u001b[m up to but not including \u001b[4mlast\u001b(B\u001b[m'.)  There was no piggy-backed ACK, the available receive window was\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 503/904 61% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
[4425.465667, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[K\u001b[?2026l\u001b[?2026h\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[A       4096 bytes and there was a max-segment-size option requesting an MSS of 1024 bytes.\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 504/904 61% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
[4425.496462, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[A\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 505/904 61% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
[4425.533716, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[A       Csam replies with a similar packet except it includes a piggy-backed ACK for rtsg's SYN.  Rtsg then ACKs csam's SYN.  The `.' means the ACK flag was set.  The packet contained  no\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 506/904 62% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
[4425.566137, "o", "\r       data so there is no data sequence number or length.  Note that the ACK sequence number is a small integer (1).  The first time \u001b[4mtcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m sees a TCP `conversation', it prints the se\u001b[?2026h\u001b[K‐\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 507/904 62% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
[4425.598645, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[A       quence number from the packet.  On subsequent packets of the conversation, the difference between the current packet's sequence number and this initial sequence number is printed.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 508/904 62% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
[4425.630637, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[A       This  means  that  sequence  numbers after the first can be interpreted as relative byte positions in the conversation's data stream (with the first data byte each direction being\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 509/904 62% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
[4426.038847, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[A       `1').  `-S' will override this feature, causing the original sequence numbers to be output.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 510/904 63% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
[4426.532086, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[A\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 511/904 63% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
[4426.563941, "o", "\r       On the 6th line, rtsg sends csam 19 bytes of data (bytes 2 through 20 in the rtsg \u001b[?2026h\u001b[K→\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[37;91H csam side of the conversation).  The PUSH flag is set in the packet.  On  the  7th  line,  csam\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 512/904 63% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
[4426.600348, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[A       says it's received data sent by rtsg up to but not including byte 21.  Most of this data is apparently sitting in the socket buffer since csam's receive window has gotten 19 bytes\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 513/904 63% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
[4426.630376, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[A       smaller.  Csam also sends one byte of data to rtsg in this packet.  On the 8th and 9th lines, csam sends two bytes of urgent, pushed data to rtsg.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 514/904 63% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
[4426.666872, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[A\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 515/904 63% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
[4426.694892, "o", "\r       If the snapshot was small enough that \u001b[4mtcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m didn't capture the full TCP header, it interprets as much of the header as it can and then reports ``[|\u001b[4mtcp\u001b(B\u001b[m]'' to indicate the remain\u001b[?2026h\u001b[K‐\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 516/904 64% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
[4426.732904, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[21;38r\u001b[38;1H\n\u001b[A       der  could  not  be  interpreted.   If the header contains a bogus option (one with a length that's either too small or beyond the end of the header), \u001b[4mtcpdump\u001b(B\u001b[m reports it as ``[\u001b[4mbad\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page tcpdump(8) line 517/904 64% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[1;38r\u001b[38;73H\u001b[?2026l"]
