[4789.715528, "o", "\u001b[2;8H\u001b[38;2;224;222;244m                                                                Overview\u001b[3;8H                                                               \u001b[4;8H             \u001b[5;8H \u001b[6;8H2.3.  Function Description                                         \u001b[7;8H                                                                     \u001b[8;8H  The function or purpose of Internet Protocol is to move datagrams\u001b[9;8H  through an interconnected set of networks.  This is done by passing \u001b[10;8H  the datagrams from one internet module to another until the       \u001b[11;8H  destination is reached.  The internet modules reside in hosts and\u001b[12;8H  gateways in the internet system.  The datagrams are routed from one\u001b[13;8H  internet module to another through individual networks based on the\u001b[14;8H  interpretation of an internet address.  Thus, one important mechanism\u001b[15;8H  of the internet protocol is the internet address.                     \u001b[16;8H                                                        \u001b[17;8H  In the routing of messages from one internet module to another,\u001b[18;8H  datagrams may need to traverse a network whose maximum packet size is\u001b[19;3H\u001b[1m607  \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;224;222;244m\u001b[48;2;38;35;58m  smaller than the size of the datagram.  To overcome this difficul\u001b[38;2;25;23;36m\u001b[48;2;149;177;172mty\u001b[38;2;224;222;244m\u001b[48;2;38;35;58m, a\u001b[20;8H\u001b[49m  fragmentation mechanism is provided in the internet protocol.     \u001b[21;8H                                                              \u001b[22;8H  Addressing                                                    \u001b[23;8H                                                         \u001b[24;8H    A distinction is made between names, addresses, and routes [4].   A\u001b[25;8H    name indicates what we seek.  An address indicates where it is.  A\u001b[26;8H    route indicates how to get there.  The internet protocol deals\u001b[27;8H    primarily with addresses.  It is the task of higher level (i.e.,\u001b[28;8H    host-to-host or application) protocols to make the mapping from\u001b[29;8H    names to addresses.   The internet module maps internet addresses to\u001b[30;8H    local net addresses.  It is the task of lower level (i.e., local net\u001b[31;8H    or gateways) procedures to make the mapping from local net addresses\u001b[32;8H    to routes.                          \u001b[33;8H \u001b[34;8H    Addresses are fixed length of four octets (32 bits).  An address\u001b[35;8H    begins with a network number, followed by local address (called the\u001b[36;8H    \"rest\" field).  There are three formats or classes of internet\u001b[37;5Hty\u001b[38;2;110;106;134mat\u001b[135C\u001b[38;2;224;222;244m                                           \u001b[7G\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[4789.719011, "o", "\u001b[19;75H\u001b[38;2;224;222;244m\u001b[48;2;38;35;58mty\u001b[37;5H\u001b[49mty\u001b[38;2;110;106;134mpes\u001b[138C\u001b[38;2;224;222;244m  \u001b[7G\u001b[?25l\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[4789.719467, "o", "\u001b[19;75H\u001b[38;2;25;23;36m\u001b[48;2;149;177;172mty\u001b[37;5H\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;224;222;244mty\u001b[38;2;110;106;134mpes\u001b[138C\u001b[38;2;224;222;244m  \u001b[7G\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[4789.865199, "o", "\b\b\u001b[38;2;224;222;244mtyp\u001b[38;2;110;106;134mes\b\b\u001b[?25l\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[4789.866106, "o", "\u001b[2;16H\u001b[38;2;224;222;244mPrecedence                                                      \u001b[4;18H111 - Network Control\u001b[5;18H110 - Internetwork Control\u001b[6;8H          101 - CRITIC/ECP\u001b[7;18H100 - Flash Override\u001b[8;10H        011 - Flash                                              \u001b[9;10H        010 - Immediate                                            \u001b[10;10H        001 - Priority                                     \u001b[11;10H        000 - Routine                                            \u001b[12;10H                                                                   \u001b[13;10H  The use of the Delay, Throughput, and Reliability indications may\u001b[14;10H  increase the cost (in some sense) of the service.  In many networks\u001b[15;10H  better performance for one of these parameters is coupled with worse\u001b[16;12Hperformance on another.  Except for very unusual cases at most two\u001b[17;10H  of these three indications should be set.                    \u001b[18;10H                                                                     \u001b[19;3H\u001b[1m931  \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;224;222;244m\u001b[48;2;38;35;58m    The \u001b[38;2;25;23;36m\u001b[48;2;149;177;172mtyp\u001b[38;2;224;222;244m\u001b[48;2;38;35;58me of service is used to specify the treatment of the datagram\u001b[20;10H\u001b[49m  during its transmission through the internet system.  Example\u001b[21;12Hmappings of the internet \u001b[48;2;50;54;63mtyp\u001b[49me of service to the actual service\u001b[22;10H  provided on networks such as AUTODIN II, ARPANET, SATNET, and PRNET\u001b[23;12His given in \"Service Mappings\" [8].\u001b[24;12H                                                                   \u001b[25;12H                                                                  \u001b[26;12H                                                              \u001b[27;8H[Page 12]                                                           \u001b[28;8H\u001b[38;2;156;207;216m^L\u001b[38;2;224;222;244m                                                                 \u001b[29;12H                                                                    \u001b[30;8HSeptember 1981                                                          \u001b[31;12H                                                   Internet Protocol\u001b[32;12H                                                       Specification\u001b[34;12H                                                                \u001b[35;12H                                                                   \u001b[36;12HThe Network Control precedence designation is intended to be used\u001b[37;5Htyp\u001b[38;2;110;106;134mes\u001b[134C\u001b[38;2;224;222;244m                                           \u001b[8G\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
