[4842.561766, "o", "\u001b[2;16H\u001b[38;2;224;222;244m                                                        Overview\u001b[4;18H                     \u001b[5;18H                          \u001b[6;8H2.3.  Function Description\u001b[7;18H                    \u001b[8;10HThe function or purpose of Internet Protocol is to move datagrams\u001b[9;10Hthrough an interconnected set of networks.  This is done by passing\u001b[10;10Hthe datagrams from one internet module to another until the\u001b[11;10Hdestination is reached.  The internet modules reside in hosts and\u001b[12;10Hgateways in the internet system.  The datagrams are routed from one\u001b[13;10Hinternet module to another through individual networks based on the\u001b[14;10Hinterpretation of an internet address.  Thus, one important mechanism\u001b[15;10Hof the internet protocol is the internet address.                     \u001b[16;12H                                                                  \u001b[17;10HIn the routing of messages from one internet module to another,\u001b[18;10Hdatagrams may need to traverse a network whose maximum packet size is\u001b[19;3H\u001b[1m607  \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;2;224;222;244m\u001b[48;2;38;35;58m  smaller than the size of the datagram.  To overcome this difficul\u001b[38;2;25;23;36m\u001b[48;2;149;177;172mty\u001b[38;2;224;222;244m\u001b[48;2;38;35;58m, a\u001b[20;10H\u001b[49mfragmentation mechanism is provided in the internet protocol.  \u001b[21;12H                                                              \u001b[22;10HAddressing                                                           \u001b[23;12H                                   \u001b[24;12HA distinction is made between names, addresses, and routes [4].   A\u001b[25;12Hname indicates what we seek.  An address indicates where it is.  A\u001b[26;12Hroute indicates how to get there.  The internet protocol deals\u001b[27;8H    primarily with addresses.  It is the task of higher level (i.e.,\u001b[28;8H    host-to-host or application) protocols to make the mapping from\u001b[29;12Hnames to addresses.   The internet module maps internet addresses to\u001b[30;8H    local net addresses.  It is the task of lower level (i.e., local net\u001b[31;12Hor gateways) procedures to make the mapping from local net addresses\u001b[32;12Hto routes.                                                          \u001b[34;12HAddresses are fixed length of four octets (32 bits).  An address\u001b[35;12Hbegins with a network number, followed by local address (called the\u001b[36;12H\"rest\" field).  There are three formats or classes of internet   \u001b[37;5Hty\u001b[137C                                           \u001b[7G\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
